From b9da99a02613b6956efd5294262bee4041c51293 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arsenova <7z0423arsenova@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:35:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] scx_lavd: Use setters for the remaining slice and
 dsq_vtime writes

On v7.2 kernels, loading scx_lavd floods the kernel log with "Writing
directly to p->scx.slice/dsq_vtime is deprecated". The verifier warns for
every direct store to these fields it checks.

Three direct writes survived the setter conversion. lavd_enqueue() sets
p->scx.dsq_vtime on the SCX_ENQ_REENQ path, and ask_cpu_yield_after()
sets the victim's slice with WRITE_ONCE() in two places. Convert them to
scx_bpf_task_set_dsq_vtime() and scx_bpf_task_set_slice().

The victim comes from __COMPAT_scx_bpf_cpu_curr() under
bpf_rcu_read_lock(), which satisfies the KF_RCU requirement of
scx_bpf_task_set_slice(). With sub-schedulers, the setter now refuses a
victim owned by another scheduler. The return value is ignored, because
the yield request is best effort, as it was before.

Fixes: 14f12ba2329a ("scx_lavd: replace deprecated ops.cpu_acquire/release with a sched_switch hook")
Fixes: e1a0b0c424d6 ("scx_lavd: Avoid using IPI on preemption.")
Fixes: d69abf0bf242 ("scx_lavd: Preempt a slice-boosted task if appropriate.")
Closes: #3852
Signed-off-by: Arsenova <7z0423arsenova@proton.me>
---
 scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/main.bpf.c    | 2 +-
 scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/preempt.bpf.c | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/main.bpf.c b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/main.bpf.c
index 0826aa59..20f6de5a 100644
--- a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/main.bpf.c
+++ b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/main.bpf.c
@@ -1008,7 +1008,7 @@ void BPF_STRUCT_OPS(lavd_enqueue, struct task_struct *p, u64 enq_flags)
 		 * deadline would over-prioritize it. Re-anchor to the current
 		 * clock.
 		 */
-		p->scx.dsq_vtime = calc_when_to_run(p, taskc);
+		scx_bpf_task_set_dsq_vtime(p, calc_when_to_run(p, taskc));
 
 		dsq_id = get_target_dsq_id(p, cpuc, taskc);
 		scx_bpf_dsq_insert_vtime(p, dsq_id, p->scx.slice,
diff --git a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/preempt.bpf.c b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/preempt.bpf.c
index 49121e66..faf4c5d5 100644
--- a/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/preempt.bpf.c
+++ b/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/src/bpf/preempt.bpf.c
@@ -248,10 +248,10 @@ static void ask_cpu_yield_after(struct cpu_ctx *victim_cpuc, u64 new_slice)
 			bool ret = __sync_bool_compare_and_swap(
 				&victim_cpuc->est_stopping_clk, old, 0);
 			if (ret)
-				WRITE_ONCE(victim_p->scx.slice, new_slice);
+				scx_bpf_task_set_slice(victim_p, new_slice);
 		} else {
 			if (victim_p->scx.slice > new_slice)
-				WRITE_ONCE(victim_p->scx.slice, new_slice);
+				scx_bpf_task_set_slice(victim_p, new_slice);
 		}
 	}
 	bpf_rcu_read_unlock();
-- 
